{"id": "sonnet__GEN__omni_2317__0", "result": "Let p_n be the probability of rain n days from today. Then p_0 = 0 and p_{n+1} = 0.75 p_n + 0.25(1 \u2212 p_n) = 0.25 + 0.5 p_n.\n\nThe fixed point is 0.5, so p_n \u2212 0.5 = (p_0 \u2212 0.5)(0.5)^n, which gives p_n = 0.5 \u2212 0.5^{n+1}.\n\nWe need p_n > 0.499, so 0.5^{n+1} < 0.001, i.e. 2^{n+1} > 1000.\n\nSince 2^10 = 1024 > 1000 and 2^9 = 512 < 1000, we need n+1 \u2265 10, so n \u2265 9.\n\nCheck n = 9: p_9 = 0.5 \u2212 1/1024 \u2248 0.49902 > 0.499. \u2713.\nCheck n = 8: p_8 = 0.5 \u2212 1/512 \u2248 0.49805 < 0.499. \u2713.\n\nANSWER: 9", "rc": 0, "cost": 0.009696, "model_used": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "secs": 10.8}